Package: spice
Title: Circuit Simulation with a 'SPICE3f5'-Derived Engine
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("André", "Leite", email = "leite@de.ufpe.br", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("The Regents of the University of California", role = "cph",
           comment = "'SPICE3f5', from which the simulation engine is derived"),
    person("The authors of the dependency Rust crates", role = "cph",
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS for details")
  )
Description: Runs 'SPICE3' circuit netlists (operating point, DC sweep,
    transient, small-signal AC, pole-zero, noise, distortion, transfer
    function and sensitivity analyses) on 'Dune', a circuit simulator
    written in 'Rust' and derived from Berkeley 'SPICE3f5', validated
    against 'ngspice'. Results come back as long tibbles ready for
    plotting, and plots can be read from and written to 'SPICE3'
    rawfiles for exchange with other simulators.
